Usage: doc-html-translate [flags] <file>

Flags may be written before or after the file; both orders mean the same thing.
A path that contains spaces needs quotes.

  -dst string
    	target language (default "ru")
  -fdsec-password-env string
    	for a FileDO secret file (.fd-sec): the name of an environment variable that holds its password (unattended runs; the console and the app window ask instead)
  -folder string
    	output folder (default: same directory as input file)
  -force
    	re-extract and re-translate even if output already exists (yes, all over again)
  -free
    	alias for -ollama: translate using local Ollama
  -google
    	translate using Google Translate API
  -max-cost float
    	abort paid translation before your wallet notices if the USD estimate exceeds N (0 = live dangerously, no limit)
  -multipage
    	produce multiple HTML pages with a table of contents instead of the default single page
  -noopen
    	do not open browser after conversion (batch mode)
  -notranslate
    	convert only, skip translation
  -ocr
    	OCR text inside document images and overlay it as translatable HTML (needs tesseract)
  -ocr-download string
    	download an OCR language pack (e.g. rus) into the per-user tessdata folder, then exit
  -ocr-lang string
    	OCR language(s) for -ocr, e.g. eng or eng+rus (default: -src, else eng)
  -ocr-langs
    	list installed and available OCR languages, then exit
  -ollama
    	translate using local Ollama (default model: gemma3:12b)
  -ollama-ctx int
    	context window size in tokens sent to Ollama (default 8192)
  -ollama-model string
    	Ollama model name (default "gemma3:12b")
  -ollama-parallel int
    	concurrent batch requests (set OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=N on Ollama side too) (default 1)
  -register
    	register app as document handler in HKCU
  -register-openwith
    	add app to the Windows "Open with" list without making it the default handler
  -report
    	pack the recent run logs plus an environment summary into an archive for the author, then exit
  -split int
    	split pages at N chars for browser GT extension (0 = disable) (default 5000)
  -src string
    	source language (default "en")
  -toc-depth int
    	table-of-contents nesting depth shown on index.html (0 = unlimited)
  -ui-lang string
    	interface language for the console output and the converted page's navigation (default: the Windows UI language); one of: en ru uk de it es fr pt ar hi bn ur zh
  -unregister
    	release the default-handler association (leaves the right-click "Convert to HTML" entry and "Open with")
  -v	verbose output - more than you ever wanted to know
  -version
    	print version and exit
